    <main>
        <h1>LeetCode 3014: Minimum Number of Pushes to Type Word I (C++)</h1>
        <div class="problem-description">
            <p><strong>Problem:</strong>
                You are given a string word containing distinct lowercase English letters. You can remap the letters to
                keys on a telephone keypad with 8 available keys (2-9), where each key can hold multiple letters. Return
                the minimum number of key presses needed to type out the entire word, assuming letters are assigned
                optimally to minimize total presses.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong>
                Input: word = "abcde"<br>
                Output: 5<br>
                Explanation: Since there are only 5 distinct letters and 8 keys, each letter can be assigned to its own
                key requiring only 1 press each, totaling 5 presses.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-container">
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyCode(this)">Copy Code</button>
            <pre><code class="language-cpp">class Solution {
public:
    int minimumPushes(string word) {
        int rem = word.size();
        int res = 0;
        while (rem &gt; 0) {
            res += rem;
            rem -= 8;
        }
        return res;
    }
};</code></pre>
